I would suggest doing the /VERIFY.  We run the following:
Sat - Thu: Incremental Backups
Fri:  Full Backup

In the past we didn't use /VERIFY. and on 2 of my MicroVAX 3190's the tapes
never were written too.  The actual root cause was the local facility never
changed tapes (same tape for over a year)  Anyway, I needed to pull a file
from backups and found there was nothing.  After that I did a /VERIFY on
everything.

At a minimum run it on your fulls.

Oh, forgot to ask, how critical is your data?  Ours is a VERY important.
The worst we can lose is the current days worth of data which is covered by
journal files.

Dave


