I run the stuff in batch.  The batch job does a search for "-E-" and
"-W-" in the batch log file and sends the results to me in an email 
which I scan each morning.  Note that /VERIFY doesn't actually correct 
any problems, it just lets you know that they exist.  Also, keep in mind 
that with /RECORD, if there is a problem with a file being locked by 
another user, then the backup date won't be written.



