> I would suggest doing the /VERIFY.  We run the following:
> Sat - Thu: Incremental Backups
> Fri:  Full Backup

Something which I do which doesn't seem to be that common is to do an 
/IMAGE/RECORD about once a month (depending on how much has changed on 
the disk) and a /NOIMAGE/NORECORD/SINCE=BACKUP daily.  That way, if the 
disk crashes, I can restore from just two tapes, not from a whole series 
as in "regular" incrementals.  Of course, with an /IMAGE daily, I just 
need one, but that is overkill for the time to do it.  Also, a lot more 
has to be scanned to recover accidentally deleted files.  I keep the 
daily tapes for a week, except Sunday's, which I keep for a month, and 
all the /IMAGEs.  For me, this maximises the ability to recover quickly 
after a crash and to retrieve lost files and minimises the time and 
storage.



