We did a 2-stage backup in our nightly cycle.

First, we did disk-to-disk backups of all the database files.  This
allowed us to get out of the backup section of our nightly cycle ASAP.

Then, once the cycle was done, we would light off a tape backup of the
on-line backups.  With all that redundancy, we didn't need /verify.
